    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full suite (`AcceptanceTest`, the only test class, 3 tests) is green with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization on owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the `POST /api/owners` handler).\n\n**New `normalizeAddress` helper** \u2014 trims, collapses internal whitespace to single spaces, upper-cases, and expands common abbreviations on a whole-word basis (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`). A `null`/whitespace-only address normalizes to `\"\"`.\n\n**Wired into `addOwner`:**\n- The address is normalized up front, and the required-field check runs against the **normalized** value, so an address that is blank after normalization (e.g. `\"   \"`) is rejected with 400.\n- The normalized address is set on the mapped `Owner` before saving, so it is **stored and returned** (`GET` echoes `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`, `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`, etc.). I set it on the `Owner` rather than the generated DTO to avoid depending on the generated setter.\n- Household duplicate detection and the shared `householdId` derivation now compare via a new `householdAddressKey` helper (`normalizeForHousehold(normalizeAddress(...))`), applied to **both** the incoming and each existing owner's address, so every address comparison uses the normalized form.\n\n`updateOwner` was left unchanged, since the spec scopes normalization to when an owner is *created*.\n\nTests verified: whitespace/case normalization, abbreviation expansion, and rejection of blank-after-normalization all pass, and no existing behavior regressed.",
